    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0676" n="588" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg588"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Barrett to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-08-02"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 2, 1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose copies of some
                    correspondence bearing directly on the port question.</p>
                <p>The first includes copies of certain letters exchanged between Governor Davis and
                    the minister of foreign affairs which the latter placed in my hands, I would
                    explain, however, that this represents <pb facs="0677" n="589" xml:id="pg589"/>
                    only a small part of the entire correspondence between these two officials,
                    copies of which General Davis has himself forwarded to Washington.</p>
                <p>The second is a new statement of the Panama argument submitted to me by the
                    minister of foreign affairs.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Barrett.</hi></signed></closer>




